NAME
    vsshd - the SSH-2 server daemon

SYNOPSIS
    vsshd

DESCRIPTION
    Serves SSH-2 remote logins on port 22: an RSA-2048 host key (the
    fixed device key embedded at build time, see hostkey.h),
    diffie-hellman-group14-sha256 key exchange, aes128-ctr with
    hmac-sha2-256, password authentication checked against /etc/passwd
    exactly the way the console login checks it, and on success a
    single session channel running the machine's own /bin/vash. No pty
    is emulated: vash edits and echoes its own lines, so the session
    is two plain byte pipes against the shell.

    The daemon is normally started and stopped by 'vnu set
    outsideaccess on|off' (see man vnu), which also records the choice
    in /etc/vnu/config/vsshd.conf. Run directly only to debug: the
    daemon refuses to start unless that file says 'outsideaccess on'.
    It writes its pid to /tmp/vsshd.pid, forks a process per accepted
    connection, and reaps the children as they finish. It stops within
    a second of the switch file flipping to off (SIGTERM is only the
    fast path), removing the pid file and exiting.

    From the host, run.sh forwards guest port 22 to host loopback
    10022, so 'ssh -p 10022 root@127.0.0.1' reaches it over the real
    NIC (slirp hostfwd) when QEMU runs with the SSH port mapped.

FILES
    /etc/vnu/config/vsshd.conf  the outside-access switch
    /tmp/vsshd.pid     the daemon's pid
    /tmp/.session      the session identity handed to /bin/vash
    /tmp/.ssh_out      the session's stdout/stderr drain file

EXIT STATUS
    0 when shutting down cleanly; 1 when the switch file forbids it or
    the socket cannot be bound.

SEE ALSO
    vnu(1) (the set command), vash(1), man passwd
